# Public UI Design Constraints

All public `client` UI follows `client/DESIGN.md`. Read it before styling work.

- Use design tokens: `bg-primary`, `bg-background`, `bg-card`, `text-foreground`,
  `text-muted-foreground`, `border-border`, `bg-tint`, `text-interactive`.
- Do NOT use raw Tailwind palette classes for chrome (`bg-blue-600`, `text-gray-900`,
  `bg-gray-50`, etc.). Semantic green/red for open/closed status is fine.
- One type family (IBM Plex Sans). Never add a second heading font.
- Surfaces: cards/panels use `rounded-lg` + `bg-card border border-border`.
  Buttons, search fields, and primary CTAs use `rounded-full`.
  Borders over shadows; `shadow-sm` max for cards, no `shadow-lg` + hover-lift.
- Motion: color/opacity/height for interaction. No decorative `hover:scale-*`,
  `hover:-translate-y-*`, animated gradients, or floating icons. Respect reduced motion.
- Buttons: one filled (`bg-primary`) and one outline/text style, both pills.
  No hover invert-to-solid-blue on chips or outline buttons.
- Signature: home full-bleed shop photo + ~80svh viewport + centered pill search.
  Below the fold: soft grain/radial atmosphere on key bands; one dark signature
  section (How It Works). Listing/search pages use navy `PageHeader` (not
  `bg-primary` slabs), pill search/filter CTAs, and a result count above grids.
  No WebGL demo backgrounds as default chrome.
  Consumer-app / SaaS product patterns are fine — not limited to “directory only.”
  Restrained flair (step numbers, tint icon wells) is fine; no rainbow icon boxes.
- Nav: Home, Browse, Resources (incl. How to Claim + FAQ), About, Contact, Search.
  Home page only: transparent nav over the hero; other pages solid light bar.

This does not apply to `internal-client` (admin UI).
